### Galactic Spacefarer Adventure — sample requests
#
# For the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ's compatible .http runner).
# `Authorization: Basic <user> <password>` is REST Client's shorthand for Basic auth — it
# base64-encodes the credentials for you, no need to do it by hand.
#
# Start the server first:  npm run watch   (serves on {{host}})
#
# Mocked users (see package.json cds.requires.auth / README.md "Security model"):
#   xavier / planetx  SpacefarerManager  Planet X
#   yvonne / planety  SpacefarerManager  Planet Y
#   vera   / vera     SpacefarerViewer   Planet X
#   zed    / galaxy   GalacticAdmin      (all planets)
#   nobody / nobody   (no role -> 403)
#
# All requests below were verified against a running `npx cds serve` on this checkout.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@base = {{host}}/odata/v4/spacefarers

### List as Xavier (Manager, Planet X) — with $count; expect 24, all rows originPlanet_code = X
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers?$count=true
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx

### List as Yvonne (Manager, Planet Y) — expect 20, all rows originPlanet_code = Y
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers?$count=true
Authorization: Basic yvonne planety

### Admin list as Zed (GalacticAdmin, all planets) — default page size 20 of 60,
### the response carries @odata.nextLink; follow it (or add $skip=20) to page further
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic zed galaxy

### Anonymous request — no Authorization header at all -> 401
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers

### Authenticated but role-less user — nobody has no galactic role -> 403
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic nobody nobody

### Create an active spacefarer directly as Xavier (IsActiveEntity: true bypasses the draft).
### Planet is defaulted to X (Xavier's own planet), onboarding bonus/call sign/certification
### are computed by the before-CREATE handlers; a client-supplied callSign is ignored.
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "IsActiveEntity": true,
  "name": "Rin Okafor",
  "email": "rin.okafor@example.com",
  "wormholeNavigationSkill": 3,
  "spacesuitColor_code": "RED",
  "callSign": "HACKED-TRY-ME"
}

### Cross-planet create: Xavier (Planet X) tries to launch a spacefarer "on" Planet Y.
### assertPlanetAllowed rejects this with 403, targeting originPlanet_code.
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "IsActiveEntity": true,
  "name": "Cross Planet Candidate",
  "email": "cross.planet@example.com",
  "spacesuitColor_code": "RED",
  "originPlanet_code": "Y"
}

### Position below the required minimum wormhole skill: Chief Navigator (b...003, dept
### Wormhole Navigation) requires skill 9; this candidate only has 2 -> 400 on
### wormholeNavigationSkill.
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "IsActiveEntity": true,
  "name": "Rookie Cadet",
  "email": "rookie.cadet@example.com",
  "spacesuitColor_code": "RED",
  "wormholeNavigationSkill": 2,
  "position_ID": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"
}

### Duplicate email: aria.voss@galactic.example already belongs to a seeded Planet X
### spacefarer -> 400 targeting email (the pre-check turns what would be a raw SQLite
### constraint error into a clean, field-targeted validation error).
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "IsActiveEntity": true,
  "name": "Duplicate Aria",
  "email": "aria.voss@galactic.example",
  "spacesuitColor_code": "RED"
}

### --- Draft flow (Yvonne, Manager on Planet Y) ---

### 1. Create a new draft. Planet defaults to Y, spacesuit color defaults to SILVER;
### none of the before-CREATE enhancements run yet (this is only a draft).
# @name draftCreate
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers
Authorization: Basic yvonne planety
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 2. Fill in the required fields on the draft with a PATCH.
PATCH {{base}}/Spacefarers(ID={{draftCreate.response.body.$.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: Basic yvonne planety
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nova Quill",
  "email": "nova.quill@example.com",
  "wormholeNavigationSkill": 5
}

### 3. Activate the draft — this runs the very same before-CREATE handlers as a direct
### POST (onboarding bonus, call sign, certification, launchedAt) and returns 201.
POST {{base}}/Spacefarers(ID={{draftCreate.response.body.$.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/SpacefarerService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic yvonne planety

### --- Editing an existing spacefarer ---

### Edit the spacesuit color of an existing, already-active spacefarer (Aria Voss, Planet X,
### seeded ID) directly — no draft needed for a plain field update; expect 200.
PATCH {{base}}/Spacefarers(ID=c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "spacesuitColor_code": "GOLD"
}

### $filter on the calculated stardustStatus element (Legendary = stardustCollection >= 10000)
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers?$filter=stardustStatus eq 'Legendary'&$select=name,stardustCollection,stardustStatus
Authorization: Basic zed galaxy

### $orderby on wormholeNavigationSkill, descending, top 5
GET {{base}}/Spacefarers?$orderby=wormholeNavigationSkill desc&$top=5&$select=name,wormholeNavigationSkill
Authorization: Basic zed galaxy

### Value list metadata: $metadata carries Common.ValueList on originPlanet_code,
### spacesuitColor_code and department_ID, pointing at Planets / SpacesuitColors / Departments
GET {{base}}/$metadata
Authorization: Basic xavier planetx
